<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 05:47:31 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Russia hits Kyiv’s Southern Bridge as Moscow continues to pound capital</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261002-live-russia-hits-kyiv-s-southern-bridge-as-moscow-continues-to-pound-capital</link><description>
Russian airstrikes hit Kyiv’s Southern Bridge, the city’s mayor said on Friday. Russia also targeted a school and apartment buildings in the capital, killing at least one person. Ukraine, meanwhile, launched an overnight drone attack on the Russian city of Volgograd, targeting industrial facilities. Follow our liveblog for all the latest developments on the war in Ukraine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bac6f0b2-be24-11f1-b3da-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26274314811352.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bac6f0b2-be24-11f1-b3da-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26274314811352.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b2737eb0-be21-11f1-999b-6f695d1eb5bf</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 05:30:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bac6f0b2-be24-11f1-b3da-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26274314811352.jpg">© Evgeniy Maloletka, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>US presses Europe to release diesel reserves 'immediately' as Trump threatens export ban</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261001-us-europe-diesel-reserves-fuel-prices</link><description>
The United States on Thursday urged European allies to release strategic diesel reserves immediately to curb prices driven higher by the US war on Iran. EU states will discuss a coordinated response on Friday, as Washington increases pressure following US President Donald Trump's suggestion that he could ban US diesel exports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0321c574-b409-11f1-a939-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T093053Z-2036940640-RC2ZINAAJOGS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-ECONOMY-ENERGY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0321c574-b409-11f1-a939-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T093053Z-2036940640-RC2ZINAAJOGS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-ECONOMY-ENERGY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9f802b5c-bde3-11f1-ad91-8d4abb1d2d7b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 22:08:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0321c574-b409-11f1-a939-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T093053Z-2036940640-RC2ZINAAJOGS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-ECONOMY-ENERGY.jpg">© Angelika Warmuth, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>UK police arrest dual UK-Iranian national over Fairford air base incident</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261001-uk-police-arrest-dual-uk-iranian-national-over-fairford-air-base-incident</link><description>
British police on Thursday arrested a British-Iranian dual national in connection with the security incident at the Fairford airbase Wednesday. Five other men initially arrested over the incidence were later released without charge on bail.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed3c1f38-bdcd-11f1-be32-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26272329512134.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed3c1f38-bdcd-11f1-be32-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26272329512134.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6dc60b56-bdcd-11f1-8c93-79702f254bd7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 19:40:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed3c1f38-bdcd-11f1-be32-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26272329512134.jpg">© Alastair Grant, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>A blessing or a curse? New Caledonia's dwindling nickel industry</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261001-a-blessing-or-a-curse-new-caledonia-s-dwindling-nickel-industry</link><description>
This Thursday October 1, the French government is holding a summit aimed at attracting investors and revitalising wealth creation in France's overseas territories. Among the assets Paris wants to highlight is New Caledonian nickel. But the industry has been severely weakened by the political deadlock and tensions that have rocked the archipelago in recent years.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/219e405e-bcec-11f1-823f-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/FR-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-NOUVELLE-CALEDONIE-NICKEL-BAIN-Lauren.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/219e405e-bcec-11f1-823f-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/FR-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-NOUVELLE-CALEDONIE-NICKEL-BAIN-Lauren.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b8773062-bcec-11f1-9b92-c3b2ade7bc8d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 14:39:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Karim YAHIAOUI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia launches major attack on Ukraine’s energy grid, causing power cuts</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261001-russia-launches-major-attack-on-ukraine-energy-grid-causing-power-cuts</link><description>
Russia launched its heaviest combined assault on Ukraine’s energy infrastructure in months on Wednesday, killing seven people and triggering emergency power cuts in Kyiv and nearby regions. The strikes came as officials warned of a difficult winter amid Russian attacks on Ukraine’s power and heating infrastructure.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/01bc8c06-bd27-11f1-9426-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C9R88CQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/01bc8c06-bd27-11f1-9426-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C9R88CQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c7a14b5c-bd3e-11f1-840a-dbe8dd8387c6</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 02:21:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/01bc8c06-bd27-11f1-9426-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C9R88CQ.jpg">© Vladyslav Musiienko, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>UK PM Burnham reopens divisive debate on rejoining EU</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260930-uk-pm-burnham-reopens-divisive-debate-on-rejoining-eu</link><description>
Andy Burnham put the idea of Britain rejoining the EU on the table on Wednesday, breaking a taboo for a UK prime minister and reopening the divisive Brexit debate. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Catherine Barnard, Professor of European Law at the University of Cambridge, says that Burnham "is sending the message that actually it's been pretty cold being on the outside of the EU so we're now looking at the alternatives".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d13d680-bd75-11f1-9982-19125f84d728/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17156968916abe1f7fb8d711-18300582.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d13d680-bd75-11f1-9982-19125f84d728/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17156968916abe1f7fb8d711-18300582.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1c642596-bd13-11f1-8d21-9dd5ded50a0a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:08:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Monte FRANCIS</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>UK PM Burnham reopens divisive debate on rejoining EU</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/uk-pm-burnham-reopens-divisive-debate-on-rejoining-eu</link><description>
Andy Burnham put the idea of Britain rejoining the EU on the table on Wednesday, breaking a taboo for a UK prime minister and reopening the divisive Brexit debate. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Catherine Barnard, Professor of European Law at the University of Cambridge, says that Burnham "is sending the message that actually it's been pretty cold being on the outside of the EU so we're now looking at the alternatives".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d13d680-bd75-11f1-9982-19125f84d728/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17156968916abe1f7fb8d711-18300582.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d13d680-bd75-11f1-9982-19125f84d728/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17156968916abe1f7fb8d711-18300582.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b4b8f964-bd10-11f1-ad1b-6da00c35a82e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:55:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>British PM alleges there are 'strong indications' Iran was involved in Fairford airbase incident</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-british-pm-alleges-there-are-strong-indications-iran-was-involved-in-fairford-airbase-incident</link><description>
UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham on Wednesday insisted that there were "strong indications" that Tehran was involved in a security incident on Sunday near an airbase in England that the US military uses in its war against Iran. The British government has still not explained the nature of the incident – in which five British men were arrested only to be later released on bail – and no explosives were found at the scene. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79072c1c-bc0a-11f1-9add-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-29T064654Z-1635109463-RC2USNAUC1I4-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-USA-FAIRFORD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79072c1c-bc0a-11f1-9add-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-29T064654Z-1635109463-RC2USNAUC1I4-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-USA-FAIRFORD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">deb4a9b0-bcfd-11f1-9520-4f451fb619c5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:01:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79072c1c-bc0a-11f1-9add-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-29T064654Z-1635109463-RC2USNAUC1I4-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-USA-FAIRFORD.jpg">© Toby Shepheard, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>UK-France 'one in, one out' migrant exchange deal is scrapped</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-uk-france-one-in-one-out-migrant-exchange-deal-is-scrapped</link><description>
A British-French agreement aimed at reducing the number of people trying to cross the English Channel in small boats has been scrapped, London said Wednesday. The pilot programme was intended to break the business model of "people smugglers" by exchanging undocumented migrants who had made the crossing for people who legally applied for asylum.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97e2e0e8-bced-11f1-9d0b-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26271435063936.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97e2e0e8-bced-11f1-9d0b-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26271435063936.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">56bf2f9a-bced-11f1-8b23-5bbf84ef822f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:12:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97e2e0e8-bced-11f1-9d0b-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26271435063936.jpg">© Jean-François Badias, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Macron says UK’s return to EU would be ‘excellent news’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-live-macron-sanchez-hold-joint-press-conference-during-french-president-s-spain-visit</link><description>
Speaking alongside Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez on Wednesday, French President Emmanuel Macron said that it would be "a good decision" if the UK decided to rejoin the European Union. The two leaders met at the Moncloa Palace in Madrid on the second day of Macron's two-day state visit to Spain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f943f80e-bcc5-11f1-9e59-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T115111Z-1926653752-RC2NTNAIQ2O3-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-FRANCE-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f943f80e-bcc5-11f1-9e59-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T115111Z-1926653752-RC2NTNAIQ2O3-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-FRANCE-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9151824c-bcc1-11f1-8b6b-c97e1a67d201</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:49:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f943f80e-bcc5-11f1-9e59-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T115111Z-1926653752-RC2NTNAIQ2O3-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-FRANCE-POLITICS.jpg">© Juan Medina, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine’s grid operator orders emergency power cuts in Kyiv after Russian strikes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-live-several-people-killed-as-russia-launches-new-round-of-strikes-on-kyiv</link><description>
Ukraine's main energy provider DTEK said it had made emergency power cuts in Kyiv as directed by the national grid operator after Russia hit the country's infrastructure in a wave of deadly drone and missile strikes. At least seven people, including a 14-year-old child, were killed in the attacks, Ukrainian authorities said. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24674c60-bcb3-11f1-9f05-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T072809Z-295841002-RC2HTNA0L0KW-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV-REGION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24674c60-bcb3-11f1-9f05-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T072809Z-295841002-RC2HTNA0L0KW-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV-REGION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">05c1083c-bc90-11f1-a138-8b66770295d1</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 05:35:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24674c60-bcb3-11f1-9f05-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T072809Z-295841002-RC2HTNA0L0KW-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV-REGION.jpg">© Valentyn Ogirenko, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Mystery over UK airbase scare as police find petrol but no explosives</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-mystery-over-uk-airbase-scare-as-police-find-quantity-of-petrol-but-no-explosives</link><description>
Britain's counter-terrorism police said ​on Tuesday that no improvised explosive devices had been found as part of an ​investigation ‌into a suspected plot targeting ⁠a British airbase used by US forces to ‌strike Iran, deepening uncertainty over the incident a day after five UK-based suspects were released on bail. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6f8c126a-bc37-11f1-9d3f-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26272438005114.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6f8c126a-bc37-11f1-9d3f-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26272438005114.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5f6d90c6-bc36-11f1-97c7-c77776d3fb00</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:05:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6f8c126a-bc37-11f1-9d3f-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26272438005114.jpg">© Alastair Grant, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Burnham sets out 'new path' for Britain, vows to seek consensus on ties with EU</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-burnham-sets-out-new-path-for-britain-vows-to-seek-consensus-on-ties-with-eu</link><description>
UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham pledged Tuesday to give Britain "a new social contract for the 21st century", reform the country's electoral system and build consensus on a new relationship with the European Union as he set out a long-term vision to tackle the UK's woes in his first speech as leader at the annual Labour party conference.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/847d9e5e-bc29-11f1-af88-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-29T153006Z-1085030387-RC22TNAJ4YFG-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-POLITICS-LABOUR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/847d9e5e-bc29-11f1-af88-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-29T153006Z-1085030387-RC22TNAJ4YFG-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-POLITICS-LABOUR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">240bcb0e-bc29-11f1-a4cb-f7d59cc60f65</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:54:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/847d9e5e-bc29-11f1-af88-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-29T153006Z-1085030387-RC22TNAJ4YFG-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-POLITICS-LABOUR.jpg">© Temilade Adelaja, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>'Putin's goal is to prolong his power in Russia': Journalist Roman Badanin</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260929-putin-s-goal-is-to-prolong-his-power-in-russia-journalist-roman-badanin</link><description>
A journalist who has spent more than 20 years investigating Russian leader Vladimir Putin and who is recognised as perhaps Russia's finest investigative journalist has told FRANCE 24 that Putin's aim with the war in Ukraine is simply to prolong his power inside Russia. Roman Badanin has just published a book, "Le Tsar en personne" or "The Tsar in person" which delves into exactly how Putin's mind works. Badanin says Putin acts like a gang member, and his attitude is that "if you beat me, I will beat you even harder". The book is so far out in Russian and French, with an English version to follow. He spoke to us in Perspective.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/722a12e0-bc02-11f1-833b-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3182824896abbb0e349c629-06537141.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/722a12e0-bc02-11f1-833b-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3182824896abbb0e349c629-06537141.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">882cb0f2-bbe4-11f1-b665-db5cfc53dabc</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:46:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia strikes two Kyiv data centres, cargo vessels in the Black Sea</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-russia-strikes-two-kyiv-data-centres-cargo-vessels-in-the-black-sea</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said Tuesday that Russia launched a wave of overnight strikes across Ukraine, hitting two foreign-flagged vessels in the Black Sea and targets in Kyiv. The strikes come as Russia ramps up its pressure campaign intended to make Ukraine buckle under near-constant bombardment of its capital and other cities.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/52cead58-bbd4-11f1-9d1c-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-02T111048Z-1278872644-RC21Z9AGZE2Z-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-GRAINS-TURKEY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/52cead58-bbd4-11f1-9d1c-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-02T111048Z-1278872644-RC21Z9AGZE2Z-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-GRAINS-TURKEY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c977200a-bbe0-11f1-b99b-77f2e91b48a3</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 10:35:57 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/52cead58-bbd4-11f1-9d1c-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-02T111048Z-1278872644-RC21Z9AGZE2Z-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-GRAINS-TURKEY.jpg">© Ukrainian Presidential Press Service via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Trump 'surprised' UK granted bail to suspects in alleged airbase terror plot</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-trump-surprised-uk-granted-bail-to-suspects-alleged-airbase-terror-plot</link><description>
US President Donald Trump said Monday he was “surprised” British police released on bail five men arrested on suspicion of a plot to attack a UK airbase. Trump added the case “might be” linked to Iran, since the base has been used by US bombers to target Iran since March. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bb6150a6-bbe2-11f1-92b7-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26271697935237.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bb6150a6-bbe2-11f1-92b7-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26271697935237.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">319718dc-bbe3-11f1-8a35-c3205610b507</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 09:12:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bb6150a6-bbe2-11f1-92b7-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26271697935237.jpg">© Alex Brandon, AP Photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Class sizes of more than 36 people': School protests continue in Paris and beyond</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-class-sizes-of-more-than-36-people-student-protests-continue-in-paris-and-beyond-1</link><description>
Teenagers in France have been blockading their schools and demonstrating since last week to protest a string of grievances. Standing in front of the Lycée Hélène Boucher, FRANCE 24 journalist Antonia Kerrigan said students there said there were "class sizes of more than 36 people". Click on the video for more. 
