An 87-year-old Madrid pensioner whose eviction became a rallying point for Spain’s housing protests will be able to return home after reaching a deal with the property’s owners, her lawyer said Monday. The agreement comes as demonstrations across the country pile pressure on Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez’s government to address soaring rents, a shortage of affordable homes and weak tenant protections. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/21b7db2a-b91a-11f1-ae34-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-23T131755Z-2084017206-RC2XONACI57G-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-HOUSING.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/21b7db2a-b91a-11f1-ae34-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-23T131755Z-2084017206-RC2XONACI57G-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-HOUSING.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bc2becb8-bb8c-11f1-81a3-87a44d24079d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:34:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/21b7db2a-b91a-11f1-ae34-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-23T131755Z-2084017206-RC2XONACI57G-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-HOUSING.jpg">© Susana Vera, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>Expert says UK air base plot 'fits into a very intense pattern we've been seeing in past two months'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260928-expert-says-uk-airbase-plot-fits-into-a-very-intense-pattern-we-ve-been-seeing-in-past-two-months</link><description>
British police said on Monday that five men arrested near an air base used by the United States were released on bail, as officers probed whether a "foreign state" could be involved in a suspected bomb plot. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Yan Saint-Pierre, CEO of Modern Security Consulting Group, explains that many of the hybrid warfare cases seen recently "involve local nationals, this is not about exporting terror", adding that foreign actors aim to have "as many layers as possible to complicate any investigation and accurate denunciation of culprits".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cdf93c34-bbff-11f1-85b8-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-11573021776abbac74c694f0-96089425.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cdf93c34-bbff-11f1-85b8-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-11573021776abbac74c694f0-96089425.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1b324e32-bb83-11f1-a78b-29a7fd847213</guid><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:25:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Monte FRANCIS</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Expert says UK air base plot 'fits into a very intense pattern we've been seeing in past two months'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/expert-says-uk-airbase-plot-fits-into-a-very-intense-pattern-we-ve-been-seeing-in-past-two-months</link><description>
British police said on Monday that five men arrested near an air base used by the United States were released on bail, as officers probed whether a "foreign state" could be involved in a suspected bomb plot. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Yan Saint-Pierre, CEO of Modern Security Consulting Group, explains that many of the hybrid warfare cases seen recently "involve local nationals, this is not about exporting terror", adding that foreign actors aim to have "as many layers as possible to complicate any investigation and accurate denunciation of culprits".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cdf93c34-bbff-11f1-85b8-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-11573021776abbac74c694f0-96089425.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cdf93c34-bbff-11f1-85b8-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-11573021776abbac74c694f0-96089425.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">315a77d8-bb7f-11f1-b340-f7c5b4d39f54</guid><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:23:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>RAF Fairford: AI-enhanced photos of suspects fuel false claims about their religion</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/raf-fairford-ai-enhanced-photos-of-suspects-fuel-false-claims-about-their-religion-1</link><description>
Five men arrested over a suspected bomb plot at RAF Fairford have been released on bail as investigations continue. Meanwhile, AI-enhanced images purporting to show their faces have gone viral, with some users claiming this "proves" the men are Muslim. SynthID confirms the sharpened images were created using OpenAI tools, meaning the AI has suggested different facial features. UK police have not disclosed any names or religion, only that the men are all British nationals. Vedika Bahl explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ab19577c-bb7c-11f1-a78f-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5205307536abad0724223a0-04593679.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ab19577c-bb7c-11f1-a78f-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5205307536abad0724223a0-04593679.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7c361b16-bb7c-11f1-8ce4-4993a1ea5c04</guid><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:55:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukrainian arms producers warn competitive edge eroding due to stringent export licence rules</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ukrainian-arms-producers-warn-competitive-edge-eroding-due-to-stringent-export-licence-rules</link><description>
Russian drones struck Ukraine's National Academy of Sciences in the historic heart of Kyiv on Monday, in the latest deadly daytime attack on the capital. Volodymyr Zelensky has long been pleading with Ukraine’s allies for more military aid to fend off Russia. But Ukrainian weapons producers say the country could be bringing in significant revenue of its own, if only they were allowed to export their products. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kyiv.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53811644-bb72-11f1-a30e-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260928-210748-211410-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53811644-bb72-11f1-a30e-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260928-210748-211410-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5893aa5c-bb72-11f1-8f0f-55a720c74ecd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:28:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Leo the moderate? Pope in France defends EU values</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260928-leo-the-moderate-pope-in-france-defends-eu-values</link><description>
There's a new pope in town and he's got very different ideas on what France's far right calls the defense of Christian civilisation. Leo XIV is concluding his trip to France in the eastern city of Metz, which is closely associated with a founding father of present-day European federalism, Robert Schuman. There, the head of the world's largest organised religion proudly stated that Europe's roots are Christian, dating back to the Romans, all the while hailing an EU model that transcends "us versus them" ideology and brushes aside "might is right" in favour of human rights and international law. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/77647dfc-bb64-11f1-8928-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-28T173849Z-1858150346-RC2HSNAISWMZ-RTRMADP-3-POPE-FRANCE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/77647dfc-bb64-11f1-8928-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-28T173849Z-1858150346-RC2HSNAISWMZ-RTRMADP-3-POPE-FRANCE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">88c26192-bb67-11f1-a0e8-5fbbd1d08be0</guid><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:49:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Pope Leo wraps up France visit, urging Europe to help combat 'lies and deceit'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260928-pope-leo-wraps-up-france-visit-urging-europe-to-help-combat-lies-and-deceit</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV urged Europe on Monday to draw from its Christian roots and tradition of dialogue to counter the "uncivilised" relations and "desire for domination" driving today's wars, as he wrapped up a four-day state visit to France that leaned heavily into politics and drew huge crowds at every turn.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ae794688-bb55-11f1-b8aa-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/8c8b2072342bcafa490eae8a7771ab9d6c1ee8ca.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ae794688-bb55-11f1-b8aa-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/8c8b2072342bcafa490eae8a7771ab9d6c1ee8ca.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">af89aa86-bb55-11f1-a027-19a9a4c285bf</guid><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 16:00:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ae794688-bb55-11f1-b8aa-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/8c8b2072342bcafa490eae8a7771ab9d6c1ee8ca.jpg">© Alberto Pizzoli, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Hybrid warfare: The threat of Russia looms over the Mediterranean</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260928-hybrid-warfare-the-threat-of-russia-looms-over-the-mediterranean</link><description>
The CIA has reportedly warned several countries that Russia is preparing to launch hybrid operations across the Mediterranean Sea. But is the risk real, or is it a form of cyber warfare?
